window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-ae24d057324a4938"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"models\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">模型</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code> 可获取对应 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"gpt-55-retirement\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"gpt-55\">GPT-5.5 退役</h2> <p>从 2026 年 10 月 14 日太平洋时间中午（19:00 UTC）起，GPT-5.5 已从使用 ChatGPT 登录的 Codex 中退役。OpenAI API 与使用 API 密钥认证的 Codex 会话不受影响。</p> <p>对于使用 ChatGPT 登录 Codex 的用户，请选择可用的替代模型：</p> <ul> <li>Plus、Pro、Business、Enterprise 和 Edu：在可用时选择 <strong>GPT-6.1 Sol</strong>（<code>gpt-6.1-sol</code>）；</li> <li>Free 和 Go：在桌面应用中可用时选择 <strong>GPT-6 Luna</strong>（<code>gpt-6-luna</code>）。</li> </ul> <p>请把工作区默认值、保存的模型设置、托管配置、自定义智能体、计划任务和脚本中的 <code>gpt-5.5</code> 一并替换。管理员准备信息请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-7d04f9ab1f4a3eeb?anchor=prepare-for-the-gpt-55-retirement\">工作区模型可用性</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-model\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">选择模型（桌面应用）</h2> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用的 Work 或 Codex 中，使用输入框下方的模型和推理控制选择可用模型，并调整推理强度。更高推理强度可能改善复杂任务的结果，但会花费更长时间并使用更多词元（token）；先从默认强度开始，需要更深入的规划或分析时再提高。</p> <p><strong>Ultra</strong> 模式会调用<a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">子智能体</a>协助处理复杂任务，适合可以拆分为多个部分的大型工作。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-model_1\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-work\">选择模型（网页端 ChatGPT Work）</h2> <p>这些建议也适用于网页端的 <strong>ChatGPT Work</strong>。使用输入框下方的模型和推理控制选择可用模型，并调整推理强度。更高推理强度可能改善复杂任务的结果，但会花费更长时间并使用更多词元；先从默认强度开始，需要更深入的规划或分析时再提高。</p> <p><strong>Ultra</strong> 模式会调用<a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">子智能体</a>协助处理复杂工作，适合可以拆分为多个部分的大型任务。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-model_2\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"cli\">选择模型（交互式 CLI）</h2> <p>在交互式 CLI 会话中，使用 <code>/model</code> 切换模型或调整推理强度。也可以在启动 Codex 时通过 <code>--model</code> 或其别名 <code>-m</code> 选择模型：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex --model gpt-6.1-sol\n</code></pre> <p>同一选项也适用于非交互运行。例如：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex exec -m gpt-6.1-sol \"Review the current changes\"\n</code></pre> <p>更高推理强度可能改善复杂任务的结果，但会花费更长时间并使用更多词元；先从默认强度开始，需要更深入的规划或分析时再提高。</p> <p><strong>Ultra</strong> 模式会调用<a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">子智能体</a>，并行处理复杂工作的不同部分；适合能够拆分成多个有意义部分的任务。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-model_3\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"ide\">选择模型（IDE 扩展）</h2> <p>使用输入框下方的模型切换器选择可用模型和推理强度。更高推理强度可能改善复杂任务的结果，但会花费更长时间并使用更多词元；先从默认强度开始，需要更深入的规划或分析时再提高。</p> <p><strong>Ultra</strong> 模式会调用<a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">子智能体</a>协助处理复杂工作，适合可以拆分为多个部分的大型任务。</p> <p><a id=\"recommended-models\"></a> <a id=\"choose-a-model-for-cloud-tasks\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">推荐模型</h2> <p>复杂编码和智能体工作流可在账户及客户端支持时使用 GPT-6.1 Sol；聚焦、可重复的任务可使用 Luna。模型可用时，在模型选择器或保存的配置中选择 <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> 或 <code>gpt-6-luna</code>。</p> <p>GPT-6.1 Sol 在复杂工作中的表现接近 Astra，但成本更低。其独立推出安排请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-61-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol</a>。</p> <p>在 ChatGPT 中，GPT-6.1 Sol、GPT-6 Sol 和 GPT-6 Luna 可用于 Work 和 Codex，但不在 Chat 中提供。GPT-5.6 Sol、GPT-5.6 Terra 和 GPT-5.6 Luna 在发布过渡期间仍然可用。选择新模型不会改变工作区权限，也不会自动授予模型访问权。</p> <p>关于 Pro $500 计划以及符合资格的 Enterprise 和 Edu 计划中 Ultrafast 模式的可用性和额度使用，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-55cdea3737e39583?anchor=ultrafast-mode\">Speed</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"gpt-6-astra\"></a> <a id=\"app-compare-models\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"astra\">Astra</h3> <p>Astra 是面向代码、应用和研究等复杂工作的能力最强模型，结合了高级推理、计算机使用能力和更强的判断力。</p> <ul> <li><strong>能力</strong>: ✦ ✦ ✦ ✦ ✦</li> <li><strong>速度</strong>: ⚡ ⚡</li> <li><strong>ChatGPT 桌面应用</strong>: 可用</li> <li><strong>ChatGPT 网页版</strong>: 可用</li> <li><strong>Codex CLI</strong>: 可用</li> <li><strong>Codex IDE 扩展</strong>: 可用</li> <li><strong>ChatGPT 额度</strong>: 可用</li> <li><strong>API 接入</strong>: 可用</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Astra · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/images/api/models/gpt-6-astra-texture.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Astra · <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/images/api/models/gpt-6-astra-texture.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <h3 id=\"61-sol\">6.1 Sol</h3> <p>Sol 在复杂工作中的表现接近 Astra，但成本更低；适合在代码、应用和文档中反复开展的长时间工作。</p> <ul> <li><strong>能力</strong>: ✦ ✦ ✦ ✦ ✦</li> <li><strong>速度</strong>: ⚡ ⚡ ⚡</li> <li><strong>桌面应用中的 Work 和 Codex</strong>: 可用</li> <li><strong>网页版 ChatGPT Work</strong>: 可用</li> <li><strong>Codex CLI</strong>: 可用</li> <li><strong>Codex IDE 扩展</strong>: 可用</li> <li><strong>ChatGPT 额度</strong>: 可用</li> <li><strong>API 接入</strong>: 可用</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">6.1 Sol · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/images/api/models/gpt-6.1-sol-texture.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>6.1 Sol · <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/images/api/models/gpt-6.1-sol-texture.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <h3 id=\"6-luna\">6 Luna</h3> <p>Luna 是效率最高的模型，适合聚焦且高频的任务，包括摘要、信息提取和聚焦编码。</p> <ul> <li><strong>能力</strong>: ✦ ✦ ✦</li> <li><strong>速度</strong>: ⚡ ⚡ ⚡ ⚡</li> <li><strong>桌面应用中的 Work 和 Codex</strong>: 可用</li> <li><strong>网页版 ChatGPT Work</strong>: 可用</li> <li><strong>Codex CLI</strong>: 可用</li> <li><strong>Codex IDE 扩展</strong>: 可用</li> <li><strong>ChatGPT 额度</strong>: 可用</li> <li><strong>API 接入</strong>: 可用</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">6 Luna · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/images/api/models/gpt-5.6-luna.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>6 Luna · <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/images/api/models/gpt-5.6-luna.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>可用性取决于发布进度、登录方式和客户端。计划权限和用量请查看<a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7\">定价</a>，Enterprise 权限请查看<a href=\"#/article/a-7d04f9ab1f4a3eeb\">工作区模型可用性</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"gpt-6.1-sol\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"gpt-61-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol</h3> <p>GPT-6.1 Sol 的推出范围包括 Plus、Pro、Business、Enterprise 和 Edu 计划，适用于桌面应用和 CLI 中的 Codex，以及网页端和移动端的 ChatGPT Work。Enterprise 和 Edu 计划默认关闭 GPT-6.1 Sol，须由管理员启用。Free 和 Go 计划不在首发范围内。</p> <p>在受支持的场景中可以使用 Standard 和 Fast 模式。Pro $500 计划，以及符合资格的 Enterprise 和 Edu 计划可以使用 Ultrafast。计划与工作区要求请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-55cdea3737e39583?anchor=ultrafast-mode\">Ultrafast 模式</a>。</p> <p>请使用 <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code>。可用控制项取决于计划、客户端和工作区设置。推理强度范围为 Light 到 Ultra；Max 和 Ultra 是否可用取决于你的设置。</p> <p>有关额度使用，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7\">定价</a>；有关如何比较该模型，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/model-selection.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">模型选择指南</a>。若要了解它与上一代 Sol 模型在 API 规格上的差异，请<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/compare?model=gpt-6.1-sol&amp;model2=gpt-6-sol\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">比较 GPT-6.1 Sol 与 GPT-6 Sol（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用和网页端 ChatGPT Work 中，可从账户可用的默认 Power 设置开始。需要更深入的推理时，转向 <strong>Smarter</strong>；需要更快、成本更低的处理时，转向 <strong>Faster</strong>。打开 <strong>Advanced</strong> 可选择特定模型、推理强度或速度。</p> <p>六种 Power 预设依次为 Luna High、GPT-6 Sol Light（此示例中选中的选项）、GPT-6 Sol Medium、Astra Light、Astra Medium 和 Astra Extra High。部分付费计划不提供 Astra Extra High。Advanced 控件仅作示意；可选项和默认值会因计划、客户端、工作区设置及发布进度而异。</p> <p><a id=\"choosing-sol-terra-and-luna\"></a> <a id=\"choosing-astra-sol-and-luna\"></a> <a id=\"app-choosing-astra-sol-and-luna\"></a> <a id=\"web-choosing-astra-sol-and-luna\"></a> <a id=\"cli-choosing-astra-sol-and-luna\"></a> <a id=\"ide-choosing-astra-sol-and-luna\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"choosing-a-model\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">选择模型</h2> <p>任务需要跨步骤、跨工具的最强能力时，选择 <strong>Astra</strong>。<strong>GPT-6.1 Sol</strong> 以低于 Astra 的成本提供接近 Astra 的表现；账户和客户端支持时，可以使用 <strong>GPT-6.1 Sol</strong>，清晰、可重复的任务则使用 <strong>Luna</strong>。</p> <p><a id=\"where-each-model-shines\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">各模型适用场景</h3> <ul> <li><strong>Astra，适合最困难的端到端工作。</strong> 对于跨代码、应用和研究、需要持续推理与判断的完整工作流，选择 Astra。为它提供定义有用结果所需的来源、模板、约束和检查。Astra 更善于提出聚焦的问题并采纳你的指导，同时始终关注最初的目标与约束；</li> <li><strong>GPT-6.1 Sol</strong>：适合重视成本、需要在代码、应用和文档中持续开展的重复长时间工作；最困难的任务仍可交给 Astra；</li> <li><strong>GPT-6 Luna，适合清晰、可重复的任务。</strong> 当你清楚好结果应是什么样时，可选择 Luna 处理具体、高吞吐量的任务，例如提取、分类、转换和结构化摘要。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"pick-a-reasoning-effort\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">选择推理强度</h3> <p>GPT-6.1 Sol 可先使用客户端提供的默认推理强度，再根据任务调整。Luna 可从 <strong>High</strong> 开始，Astra 可从 <strong>Light</strong> 开始；在配置中，Astra 的 Light 对应 <code>low</code>。需要更多规划、分析或检查时再提高强度。</p> <ul> <li>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用、网页端 ChatGPT Work 和 IDE 扩展中使用 <strong>Light</strong>，在 CLI 中使用 <strong>Low</strong>：适合快速、范围明确的任务；</li> <li><strong>Medium</strong>：适用于需要更多规划的任务，在速度和深度之间平衡；</li> <li><strong>High / Extra High</strong>：包含多个步骤、来源或权衡的困难任务。</li> </ul> <p>模型代际之间的推理强度并非一一对应。可以先用熟悉的任务尝试较低设置，再根据结果调整。</p> <p><a id=\"know-when-to-use-max-or-ultra\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"max-ultra\">何时使用 Max 或 Ultra</h3> <p><strong>Max</strong> 会给所选模型更多时间来推理单个任务。适用于最困难的问题，尤其是深度比速度或用量更重要时。如果你在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中看不到 Max，请检查应用设置。</p> <p><strong>Ultra</strong> 会使用<a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">子智能体</a>并行处理复杂任务中相互独立的部分。只有在能够把任务拆分为有意义的部分时才选择 Ultra；大多数任务不需要 Max 或 Ultra。</p> <p>GPT-6 Luna 的推理强度最高支持 <strong>Max</strong>，不支持 <strong>Ultra</strong>。如果你的模型支持 Ultra，但它没有出现在桌面应用的模型滑块中，请前往 <strong>设置 &gt; 配置</strong>，然后启用 <strong>在模型选择器滑块中显示 Ultra</strong>。</p> <p>在 CLI 中，使用 <code>/model</code> 选择模型，再选择 <strong>More reasoning…</strong>，即可查看该模型支持的 Max 或 Ultra 选项。</p> <p><a id=\"other-models\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">其他模型</h2> <p>登录 ChatGPT 时，Codex 最适合使用上面列出的推荐模型。</p> <p>使用 API 密钥进行身份验证时，可用模型取决于你的 API 组织和项目。GPT-5.5 仍可通过 OpenAI API 使用，也可在使用 API 密钥认证的 Codex 会话中使用。请参阅 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">API 模型目录</a>。</p> <p>如果要使用自定义模型提供商或网关，请选择兼容的 Responses API 端点。有关配置，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85?anchor=custom-model-providers\">自定义模型提供商</a>；有关流式传输、工具和对话要求，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">网关兼容性</a>。当前 Codex 版本不支持 <code>wire_api = \"chat\"</code>，也不支持仅有 Chat Completions 的端点。</p> <p><a id=\"deprecated-codex-models\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">已弃用的 Codex 模型</h2> <p>GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark 已于 2026 年 9 月 14 日退役，不再提供给 ChatGPT 桌面应用、Codex CLI 或 IDE 扩展。请更新选择 <code>gpt-5.3-codex-spark</code> 的已保存配置、自定义智能体和脚本，改用<a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=recommended-models\">可用模型</a>。另请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-04895d13e978a931?sectionMissing=codex-2026-09-14-codex-spark-deprecation\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">Spark 退役公告</a>（官网章节，需联网） <a href=\"#/article/a-04895d13e978a931\">本地页面（官方来源暂不可用）</a>。</p> <p>使用 ChatGPT 登录时，GPT-5.5 自 2026 年 10 月 14 日太平洋时间中午（19:00 UTC）起从 Codex 退役。请将 <code>gpt-5.5</code> 替换为账户和客户端可用的模型。API 密钥认证的会话不受影响。有关不同计划的替代方案和迁移清单，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-55-retirement\">GPT-5.5 退役说明</a>。</p> <p>使用 ChatGPT 登录时，<code>gpt-5.4</code> 和 <code>gpt-5.4-mini</code> 已于 2026 年 8 月 31 日从 Codex 退役。若计划和客户端支持，请将 <code>gpt-5.4</code> 替换为 <code>gpt-6-sol</code>，并将 <code>gpt-5.4-mini</code> 替换为 <code>gpt-6-luna</code>。Enterprise 和 Edu 需要管理员先启用 Luna。请同时更新工作区默认值、已保存的模型设置、受管配置、自定义智能体和计划任务。</p> <p><code>gpt-5.2</code> 和 <code>gpt-5.3-codex</code> 在 ChatGPT 登录的 Codex 中也已弃用。请更新仍引用它们的脚本、配置文件和 <code>codex exec --model</code> 命令。</p> <p>OpenAI API 以及使用 API key 认证的 Codex 不受 GPT-5.4 退役影响。当前 API 模型可用性请查看 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">API 模型页</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-your-default-local-model\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">配置本地默认模型</h2> <p>ChatGPT 桌面应用、Codex CLI 和 IDE 扩展使用同一个 <code>config.toml</code> 配置文件。加入 <code>model</code> 条目即可指定模型；省略时使用推荐模型：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model = \"gpt-6.1-sol\"\n</code></pre> <p>如果未在配置文件中指定模型，ChatGPT 桌面应用、Codex CLI 或 IDE 扩展会使用推荐模型。配置文件位置和基本设置请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">配置基础</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"models\">Models</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"gpt-55-retirement\">GPT-5.5 retirement</h2> <p>Effective October 14, 2026, at noon PDT (19:00 UTC), GPT-5.5 retires from Codex for users signed in with ChatGPT. The OpenAI API and Codex sessions authenticated with an API key aren't affected.</p> <p>For Codex with ChatGPT sign-in, choose an available replacement:</p> <ul> <li>On Plus, Pro, Business, Enterprise, and Edu plans, choose <strong>GPT-6.1 Sol</strong> (<code>gpt-6.1-sol</code>) when available.</li> <li>On Free and Go plans, choose <strong>GPT-6 Luna</strong> (<code>gpt-6-luna</code>) in the desktop app when available.</li> </ul> <p>Replace <code>gpt-5.5</code> in workspace defaults, saved model settings, managed configurations, custom agents, scheduled tasks, and scripts that select a model.</p> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-7d04f9ab1f4a3eeb?anchor=prepare-for-the-gpt-55-retirement\">workspace model availability</a> for administrator guidance.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"choose-a-model\">Choose a model</h2> <p>In Work or Codex in the ChatGPT desktop app, use the model and reasoning control beneath the composer to choose an available model and adjust its reasoning effort.</p> <p>Higher reasoning effort can improve results for complex tasks, but it takes longer and uses more tokens. Start with the default effort and increase it when the task needs deeper planning or analysis.</p> <p><strong>Ultra</strong> mode goes beyond a single-agent run. It uses <a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">subagents</a> to accelerate complex work, making it useful for larger tasks that can be split across subagents.</p> <p class=\"notice\">This part of the official page contains an interactive demo. Open the official source online to view it.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-a-model_1\">Choose a model</h2> <p>These recommendations apply to <strong>ChatGPT Work</strong> on the web. Use the model and reasoning control beneath the composer to choose an available model and adjust its reasoning effort.</p> <p>Higher reasoning effort can improve results for complex tasks, but it takes longer and uses more tokens. Start with the default effort and increase it when the task needs deeper planning or analysis.</p> <p><strong>Ultra</strong> mode goes beyond a single-agent run. It uses <a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">subagents</a> to accelerate complex work, making it useful for larger tasks that can be split across subagents.</p> <p class=\"notice\">This part of the official page contains an interactive demo. Open the official source online to view it.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-a-model_2\">Choose a model</h2> <p>In an interactive CLI session, use <code>/model</code> to switch models or adjust reasoning effort. You can also choose a model when you launch Codex with <code>--model</code> or its <code>-m</code> alias:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex --model gpt-6.1-sol\n</code></pre> <p>The same option works with non-interactive runs. For example:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex exec -m gpt-6.1-sol \"Review the current changes\"\n</code></pre> <p>Higher reasoning effort can improve results for complex tasks, but it takes longer and uses more tokens. Start with the default effort and increase it when the task needs deeper planning or analysis.</p> <p><strong>Ultra</strong> mode goes beyond a single-agent run. It uses <a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">subagents</a> to accelerate complex work, making it useful for larger tasks that can be split across subagents.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"choose-a-model_3\">Choose a model</h2> <p>Use the model switcher below the composer to choose an available model and reasoning effort.</p> <p>Higher reasoning effort can improve results for complex tasks, but it takes longer and uses more tokens. Start with the default effort and increase it when the task needs deeper planning or analysis.</p> <p><strong>Ultra</strong> mode goes beyond a single-agent run. It uses <a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">subagents</a> to accelerate complex work, making it useful for larger tasks that can be split across subagents.</p> <p class=\"notice\">This part of the official page contains an interactive demo. Open the official source online to view it.</p> <p><a id=\"recommended-models\"></a> <a id=\"other-models\"></a> <a id=\"deprecated-codex-models\"></a> <a id=\"configure-your-default-local-model\"></a> <a id=\"choose-a-model-for-cloud-tasks\"></a> <a id=\"gpt-6-astra\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,web,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"recommended-models\">Recommended models</h2> <p>For complex coding and agentic workflows, use GPT-6.1 Sol when available to your account and client. Use Luna for focused, repeatable tasks. Select <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> or <code>gpt-6-luna</code> in your model picker or saved configuration when available.</p> <p>GPT-6.1 Sol offers near-Astra performance for complex work at a lower cost than Astra. See <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-61-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol</a> for its separate rollout.</p> <p>In ChatGPT, GPT-6.1 Sol, GPT-6 Sol, and GPT-6 Luna are available in Work and Codex. They aren't available in Chat.</p> <p>GPT-5.6 Sol, GPT-5.6 Terra, and GPT-5.6 Luna remain available during the rollout. Selecting a new model doesn't change workspace permissions or grant access to it.</p> <p>For Ultrafast mode availability and credit usage on Pro $500 and eligible Enterprise and Edu plans, see <a href=\"#/article/a-55cdea3737e39583?anchor=ultrafast-mode\">Speed</a>.</p> <p><a id=\"app-compare-models\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"astra\">Astra</h3> <p>Our most capable model for complex work across code, apps, and research, combining advanced reasoning, computer use, and stronger judgment.</p> <ul> <li><strong>Capability</strong>: ✦ ✦ ✦ ✦ ✦</li> <li><strong>Speed</strong>: ⚡ ⚡</li> <li><strong>ChatGPT desktop app</strong>: true</li> <li><strong>ChatGPT web</strong>: true</li> <li><strong>Codex CLI</strong>: true</li> <li><strong>Codex IDE extension</strong>: true</li> <li><strong>ChatGPT Credits</strong>: true</li> <li><strong>API Access</strong>: true</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Astra · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/images/api/models/gpt-6-astra-texture.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Astra · <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/images/api/models/gpt-6-astra-texture.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h3 id=\"61-sol\">6.1 Sol</h3> <p>Near-Astra performance for complex work at a lower cost than Astra. Consider it for repeated, long-running work across code, apps, and documents.</p> <ul> <li><strong>Capability</strong>: ✦ ✦ ✦ ✦ ✦</li> <li><strong>Speed</strong>: ⚡ ⚡ ⚡</li> <li><strong>Work and Codex in the desktop app</strong>: true</li> <li><strong>ChatGPT Work on the web</strong>: true</li> <li><strong>Codex CLI</strong>: true</li> <li><strong>Codex IDE extension</strong>: true</li> <li><strong>ChatGPT Credits</strong>: true</li> <li><strong>API Access</strong>: true</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">6.1 Sol · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/images/api/models/gpt-6.1-sol-texture.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>6.1 Sol · <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/images/api/models/gpt-6.1-sol-texture.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h3 id=\"6-luna\">6 Luna</h3> <p>Our most efficient model for focused, high-volume tasks, including summarization, extraction, and focused coding.</p> <ul> <li><strong>Capability</strong>: ✦ ✦ ✦</li> <li><strong>Speed</strong>: ⚡ ⚡ ⚡ ⚡</li> <li><strong>Work and Codex in the desktop app</strong>: true</li> <li><strong>ChatGPT Work on the web</strong>: true</li> <li><strong>Codex CLI</strong>: true</li> <li><strong>Codex IDE extension</strong>: true</li> <li><strong>ChatGPT Credits</strong>: true</li> <li><strong>API Access</strong>: true</li> </ul> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">6 Luna · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/images/api/models/gpt-5.6-luna.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>6 Luna · <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/images/api/models/gpt-5.6-luna.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>Availability depends on the rollout, your sign-in method, and your client. See <a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7\">pricing</a> for plan access and usage, and <a href=\"#/article/a-7d04f9ab1f4a3eeb\">workspace model availability</a> for Enterprise access.</p> <p><a id=\"gpt-6.1-sol\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"gpt-61-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol</h3> <p>The GPT-6.1 Sol launch rollout includes Plus, Pro, Business, Enterprise, and Edu in Codex in the desktop app and CLI, and ChatGPT Work on the web and mobile. For Enterprise and Edu, the plan keeps GPT-6.1 Sol off by default until an administrator enables it. Free and Go are not included at launch.</p> <p>Standard and Fast modes are available where supported. Ultrafast is available on Pro $500 and eligible Enterprise and Edu plans. See <a href=\"#/article/a-55cdea3737e39583?anchor=ultrafast-mode\">Ultrafast mode</a> for plan and workspace requirements.</p> <p>Use <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code>. Available controls depend on your plan, client, and workspace settings. Reasoning effort ranges from Light to Ultra. Max and Ultra depend on your settings.</p> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-24e0a6ab1e90e5b7\">pricing</a> for credit usage and <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/model-selection.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">model selection</a> for guidance on comparing it with Astra and Luna. To see how its API specifications differ from the previous Sol model, <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/compare?model=gpt-6.1-sol&amp;model2=gpt-6-sol\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">compare GPT-6.1 Sol and GPT-6 Sol (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</p> <p>In the ChatGPT desktop app and ChatGPT Work on the web, start with the default Power setting available to your account. Move toward <strong>Smarter</strong> for deeper reasoning or <strong>Faster</strong> for faster, lower-cost work. Open <strong>Advanced</strong> to choose a specific model, reasoning effort, or speed.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,web,cli,ide</strong></p> <p><strong>Surface: app,web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>The six Power presets shown are Luna High, GPT-6 Sol Light (selected in this example), GPT-6 Sol Medium, Astra Light, Astra Medium, and Astra Extra High. Some paid plans omit Astra Extra High. Advanced controls are illustrative; available options and defaults vary by plan, client, workspace settings, and rollout.</p> <p><a id=\"choosing-sol-terra-and-luna\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"choosing-astra-sol-and-luna\"></a> <a id=\"app-choosing-astra-sol-and-luna\"></a> <a id=\"web-choosing-astra-sol-and-luna\"></a> <a id=\"cli-choosing-astra-sol-and-luna\"></a> <a id=\"ide-choosing-astra-sol-and-luna\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"choosing-a-model\">Choosing a model</h2> <p>Choose <strong>Astra</strong> when a task needs the strongest capability across steps and tools. <strong>GPT-6.1 Sol</strong> offers near-Astra performance at a lower cost than Astra. Use <strong>GPT-6.1 Sol</strong> when available to your account and client, and <strong>Luna</strong> for clear, repeatable tasks.</p> <h3 id=\"where-each-model-shines\">Where each model shines</h3> <ul> <li><strong>Astra, for the hardest end-to-end work.</strong> Choose Astra for complete workflows across code, apps, and research that need sustained reasoning and judgment. Give it the sources, templates, constraints, and checks that define a useful result. Astra is better at asking focused questions and incorporating your guidance while keeping the original goal and constraints in view.</li> <li><strong>GPT-6.1 Sol, for repeated, long-running work.</strong> Consider GPT-6.1 Sol for work across code, apps, and documents when cost matters. Keep Astra for your most demanding work.</li> <li><strong>Luna, for clear, repeatable tasks.</strong> Choose Luna for specific, high-volume tasks when you know what a good result looks like, such as extraction, classification, transformation, and structured summaries.</li> </ul> <h3 id=\"pick-a-reasoning-effort\">Pick a reasoning effort</h3> <p>For GPT-6.1 Sol, start with the reasoning effort available by default in your client and adjust based on the task. Start with <strong>High</strong> for Luna or <strong>Light</strong> for Astra. In configuration, Astra's Light setting is <code>low</code>. Increase the effort for tasks that need more planning, analysis, or checking.</p> <ul> <li><strong>Light</strong> in the ChatGPT desktop app, ChatGPT Work on the web, and IDE extension, or <strong>Low</strong> in the CLI, suits quick, well-scoped tasks.</li> <li><strong>Medium</strong> balances speed and depth for tasks that need more planning.</li> <li><strong>High</strong> and <strong>Extra High</strong> suit difficult work with multiple steps, sources, or tradeoffs.</li> </ul> <p>Reasoning efforts don't map exactly between model generations. Try a familiar task at a lower setting and adjust based on the result.</p> <h3 id=\"know-when-to-use-max-or-ultra\">Know when to use Max or Ultra</h3> <p><strong>Max</strong> gives the selected model more time to reason about a single task. Use it for the hardest problems, when depth matters more than speed or usage. If you don't see Max in the ChatGPT desktop app, check your app settings.</p> <p><strong>Ultra</strong> uses <a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">subagents</a> to handle separate parts of a complex task in parallel. Choose it when you can divide the work into meaningful parts. Most tasks do not need Max or Ultra.</p> <p>GPT-6 Luna supports reasoning efforts up to <strong>Max</strong>, but not <strong>Ultra</strong>.</p> <p>In the CLI, use <code>/model</code>, choose a model, then select <strong>More reasoning…</strong> to see its supported Max or Ultra options.</p> <p>If your model supports Ultra but it doesn't appear in the desktop app's model slider, go to <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Configuration</strong>, then turn on <strong>Ultra in model picker slider</strong>.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"other-models\">Other models</h2> <p>With API-key authentication, model availability follows your API organization and project. GPT-5.5 remains available through the OpenAI API and in Codex sessions authenticated with an API key. See the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">API model catalog</a>.</p> <p>For a custom model provider or gateway, use a compatible Responses API endpoint. See <a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85?anchor=custom-model-providers\">Custom model providers</a> for configuration and <a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">Gateway compatibility</a> for streaming, tool, and conversation requirements. Current Codex releases don't support <code>wire_api = \"chat\"</code> or a Chat Completions-only endpoint.</p> <h2 id=\"deprecated-codex-models\">Deprecated Codex models</h2> <p>GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark retired on September 14, 2026, and is no longer available in the ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, or IDE extension. Update saved configurations, custom agents, and scripts that select <code>gpt-5.3-codex-spark</code> to use an <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=recommended-models\">available model</a>. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-04895d13e978a931?sectionMissing=codex-2026-09-14-codex-spark-deprecation\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">Spark retirement notice</a> (official section, online) <a href=\"#/article/a-04895d13e978a931\">Local page (official source unavailable)</a>.</p> <p>GPT-5.5 retires from Codex with ChatGPT sign-in on October 14, 2026, at noon PDT (19:00 UTC). Replace <code>gpt-5.5</code> with a model available to your account and client. API-key sessions aren't affected. See <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-55-retirement\">GPT-5.5 retirement</a> for plan-specific replacements and the migration checklist.</p> <p>The <code>gpt-5.4</code> and <code>gpt-5.4-mini</code> models retired from Codex with ChatGPT sign-in on August 31, 2026. Replace <code>gpt-5.4</code> with <code>gpt-6-sol</code> and <code>gpt-5.4-mini</code> with <code>gpt-6-luna</code> when available to your plan and client. In Enterprise and Edu, an administrator must enable Luna first. Update workspace defaults, saved model settings, managed configurations, custom agents, and scheduled tasks with an available replacement.</p> <p>The <code>gpt-5.2</code> and <code>gpt-5.3-codex</code> models are already deprecated in Codex when you sign in with ChatGPT. Update scripts, configuration files, and <code>codex exec --model</code> commands that still reference those models.</p> <p>The OpenAI API and Codex authenticated with your own API key aren't affected by the GPT-5.4 retirement. For current API model availability, see the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">API models page</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"configure-your-default-local-model\">Configure your default local model</h2> <p>The ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, and IDE extension use the same <code>config.toml</code> <a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">configuration file</a>. To specify a model, add a <code>model</code> entry to your configuration file. If you don't specify a model, the ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, or IDE extension uses a recommended model.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model = \"gpt-6.1-sol\"\n</code></pre>"};
